				<r3d:repositoryUrl>http://www.jive.eu/select-experiment</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">The European VLBI Network (EVN) is an interferometric array of radio telescopes located primarily in Europe and Asia, with additional telescopes in South Africa and Puerto Rico.  The EVN performs high-resolution observations of cosmic radio sources at wavelenghts from 92cm to 7mm.  The EVN Data Archive contains, among other things, the correlated data from EVN observations plus pipeline output, including the initial calibration tables to apply to the correlated data and preliminary images.  In general, the correlated data and some pipeline results are proprietary for one year following distribution to the PI of the final epoch of observations resulting from a proposal after which the data enters the public domain; more details are in the &quot;EVN Data Access Policy&quot; linked via the archive-introduction page.</r3d:description>
